.TH DESGRANA 1 "2026-10-12" "desgrana 1.13.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
desgrana \- extract channels from Wing and X32 multitrack WAV recordings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B desgrana
\fI<session-dir>\fR|\fI<file.wav>\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B desgrana
extracts individual mono or stereo tracks from the interleaved multichannel
WAV files produced by a Behringer Wing or X32 console (W\-Live, X\-Live
or card recorder), or from a single multichannel WAV file.
.PP
It reads session metadata from \fISE_LOG.BIN\fR, channel names and stereo
pairs from a console snapshot (Wing \fI.snap\fR or X32 \fI.scn\fR), skips
silent channels automatically, and writes session markers as cue chunks in
every output WAV, plus CSV, text and Standard MIDI File (type 0) exports.
Output WAVs carry iXML track names and bext provenance metadata.
Files larger than 4 GB are read and written as RF64.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output \fI<path>\fR
Output directory (default: \fI<session-dir>_extract/\fR).
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-prefix \fI<string>\fR
Prefix for output filenames.
.TP
.B \-\-snap \fI<file>\fR
Console snapshot (Wing \fI.snap\fR or X32 \fI.scn\fR) for channel names and
stereo pairs. Auto-detected if present in the session directory.
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-stereo \fI<pairs>\fR
Stereo pairs, e.g. \fI1:2,3:4\fR. Overrides pairs from the snapshot.
.TP
.B \-\-short\-names
Use the channel name only for filenames (e.g. \fIKICK.wav\fR instead of
\fIprefix_ch01_KICK.wav\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be extracted without writing any files.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print a machine-readable JSON report on stdout. Combines with
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR and \fB\-\-info\fR.
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-info
Show session info only, without extracting.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Bad arguments or session directory not found.
.TP
.B 2
Filesystem error (cannot read input or write output).
.TP
.B 3
Format error (invalid WAV, channel count mismatch between takes).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B desgrana /media/SD/X_LIVE/4B5C62B0
Extract all channels from the session directory.
.TP
.B desgrana /media/SD/X_LIVE/4B5C62B0 \-\-info
Show session metadata without extracting.
.TP
.B desgrana /media/SD/X_LIVE/4B5C62B0 \-\-snap ~/MyShow.snap \-o ~/Desktop/extract
Extract using a named snapshot file, writing to a custom output path.
.TP
.B desgrana /media/SD/X_LIVE/4B5C62B0 \-\-dry\-run \-\-json
Print the extraction plan as JSON, without writing files.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <session-dir>/SE_LOG.BIN
Session metadata: channel count, sample rate, take sizes, markers.
.TP
.I <session-dir>/*.snap, <session-dir>/*.scn
Console snapshot (optional): channel names, stereo pairs.
.TP
.I <session-dir>/00000001.WAV, 00000002.WAV, \&...
Interleaved multichannel WAV takes.
.SH AUTHOR
Romain d'Alverny <rwx@romaindalverny.com>
.SH SEE ALSO
